@harej I like the idea of adding this data a lot. I don't love removing the Wikipedia article title, though -- with the title, data users can generally quickly and reliably make a valid Wikipedia link by appending it after `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/`.

The ideal would be that your Wikidata bot keeps the Wikidata field up to date, and drops the current associated Wikipedia article title next to it at the same time. It's okay if the Wikipedia article title isn't 100% guaranteed to work, that can be a known risk for users -- and those who want the higher % of accuracy (basically anyone who wants to do anything other than quick and dirty link construction) can use the Wikidata IDs as intended.

